  "description": "BRAR_NQ is a neuroimaging dataset investigating the neural correlates of Quranic recitation. The study explores the brain's reward and anti-reward circuitry during exposure to melodic recitation of the Quran, utilizing magnetoencephalography (MEG) to uncover the neural mechanisms underlying this unique auditory-linguistic experience.",
